## FlightLeg
No explicit primary key — identity is the composite (flight_id, leg_number).
Legs are ordered by leg_number within a flight. Each leg has its own origin/destination pair.
Two FKs to Airport on the same entity: origin and destination represent the leg's endpoints.

## Flight
Two FKs to Airport: origin (departure airport) and destination (arrival airport).
These are semantically distinct — origin ≠ destination is enforced by application logic.

## Reservation
Composite unique on (passenger_name, flight_id, booking_date) prevents double-booking.
Seat is nullable — assigned at check-in, not at booking time.
